          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'The object is to win the last (fifth) trick of each hand. There are no trumps. The player who wins the last trick scores points: 3 if the winning card is a 6, 2 if a 7, and 1 if 8 or higher. The session continues for as long as players wish with no fixed target score.',
          gameplay: "Player to dealer's left leads any card. Others must follow suit if possible; if not, any card. Highest card of the suit led wins the trick. Cards stay in a face-up pile. Trick winner leads to the next trick. Five tricks per hand. Winner of the last trick scores: 3 points if winning card is a 6, 2 if a 7, 1 if 8 or higher. Winner of the hand deals the next hand.",
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit if possible; otherwise any card.',
            'Highest card of led suit wins the trick.',
            'Winner of the last trick scores 3 (with 6), 2 (with 7), or 1 (with 8 or higher) point(s).',
            'Winner of the hand deals next; no fixed target score, session continues as players wish.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Save your high cards (Aces/Kings) for the end. Winning the last trick is crucial. Don't waste an Ace early on a trick worth nothing.",
          intermediate: 'Counting Suits: Since the deck is small, knowing when a suit is exhausted is easy. Lead a long suit to force opponents to discard their high cards in other suits.',
          advanced: "The 'Spar' Bluff: Pretend to be weak to induce a lead, then slam your Ace down on the last trick.",
          tips: [
            'Winning the last trick with a 6 scores 3 points; with a 7 scores 2; with 8 or higher scores 1.',
            'Lead to force opponents to spend high cards when you cannot win the trick.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
